## 7. Parameter Tuning

The following parameters must be tuned based on hardware and environment:

- **Motor RPM** – higher RPM requires lower speed values  
- **Robot Mass** – heavier robots need more torque and delay  
- **Battery Voltage** – higher voltage increases motor speed  
- **Surface Friction & Sensor Placement** – affects correction strength  

---

## 8. Testing and Results

Each mode was tested individually:

- Manual control was responsive and stable  
- Line follower worked reliably on high-contrast tracks  
- Obstacle avoidance successfully detected and avoided objects  
- Gyro mode significantly reduced drift  
- Voice commands worked reliably in low-noise environments  

The robot performed consistently across different modes with smooth transitions.

